1:53:42 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 77447ms :: {"response":"Okay, here’s a sample muscle building diet plan tailored for you, Mani. Remember that individual results may vary depending on factors like genetics, training intensity, sleep quality, etc. It's always best to consult with a registered dietitian or certified personal trainer for more individualized guidance. Also note that since there isn't information about creatinine level given, I will make assumptions regarding creatine levels being normal.\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast\n*   **Food:** Oats Porridge (1 cup cooked) with milk(1 glass) , almonds (1 tbsp), and berries (half cup).\n*   **Portion Size**: As indicated above. Calories approximately 450 kcal\n    *   Oats provide complex carbohydrates for sustained energy. Milk adds protein and calcium. Almonds offer healthy fats and magnesium. Berries contribute antioxidants and fiber.\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack\n*   **Food:** Greek Yogurt (1 container - plain, non-fat) mixed with honey (1 tsp) and chia seeds (1 tbsp).\n*   **Portion Size**: As indicated above. Calories approximately 250 kcal\n    *   Greek yogurt provides high-quality casein protein which digests slowly overnight. Honey offers quick glucose while Chia Seeds contain omega-3s and fibre.\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch\n*   **Food:** Chicken Breast Curry (grilled chicken breast – 150 g) served with brown rice (1 cup cooked) and steamed broccoli (1 cup).\n*   **Portion Size**: As indicated above. Calories approximately 650 kcal\n    *   Chicken breast is rich in lean protein essential for muscle repair and growth. Brown Rice supplies slow digesting carbs. Broccoli gives vitamins and minerals along with some fibres.\n\n## 🌆 Evening Snack\n*   **Food:** Cottage Cheese (1 block – low fat) with cucumber slices.\n*   **Portion Size**: As indicated above. Calories approximately 200 kcal\n    *   Cottage cheese contains whey protein, another excellent source of amino acids. Cucumber helps keep hydrated.\n\n## 🌙 Dinner\n*   **Food:** Fish (salmon fillet – 120 g) baked with lemon juice and herbs, accompanied by quinoa salad (1 cup cooked) containing chickpeas, bell peppers, and olives.\n*   **Portion Size**: As indicated above. Calories approximately 600 kcal\n    * Salmon has good amount of Omega 3 Fatty Acids . Quinoa Salad provides plant-based protein from chickpeas and added nutrients from various veggies.\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n*   Processed snacks, sugary drinks, large amounts of unhealthy fats (fried foods, butter), excessive consumption of simple carbohydrates (white bread, pasta made from Maida flour). Alcohol should also be limited.\n\n## 💡 Why This Plan\n*   Protein Intake: The primary focus is on increasing protein intake through sources such as chicken, fish, greek yoghurt, cottage cheese, and lentils. Aiming for around 1.6-2.2 grams of protein per kilogram of bodyweight daily would support muscle synthesis.\n*   Carbohydrate Timing: Carbohydrates are strategically placed around workouts to fuel performance and replenish glycogen stores. Complex carbohydrates like oatmeal, brown rice, and quinoa are preferred over processed options.\n*   Healthy Fats: Healthy fats come from sources like salmon, avocados, nuts, and olive oil. These aid hormone production and overall health.\n*   Hydration: Staying well-hydrated throughout the day supports optimal bodily functions including nutrient transport and waste removal. Drink plenty of water!\n\n[MACROS: Protein 40%, Carbs 30%, Fat 30%]","followUpQuestions":[]}
